---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Directory"
	description="Personal websites and blogs from people Dominic Kennedy knows and follows."
>
	<section class="index-page content-container">
		<h1 class="page-heading text-3xl">Directory</h1>

		<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
			If my website were a social media page, this would be my "following" list:
			personal websites and blogs from the people I keep up with in my real
			life. Feeling FOMO about not being on the list?
			<a class="text-link" href="https://joachimkennedy.com/p/blog-for-me/"
				>Start your own blog</a
			>!
		</p>

		<ul
			class="mt-8 list-disc space-y-4 pl-6 leading-7 text-neutral-700 marker:text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-300 dark:marker:text-neutral-600"
		>
			<li>
				<a class="text-link font-medium" href="https://joachimkennedy.com/"
					>Joa</a
				>, my older brother's blog, is active, humorous, topically diverse, and
				relatable.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a class="text-link font-medium" href="https://magdalenekennedy.com/"
					>Maggie</a
				>, my blogless older sister's portfolio site, hosts her coolest
				projects.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a class="text-link font-medium" href="https://johnallbritten.com/"
					>John</a
				>, a friend from undergrad, posts book reviews.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a class="text-link font-medium" href="https://jacobarmiger.vercel.app/"
					>Jacob</a
				>, a friend from undergrad, posts book reviews and personal projects.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a class="text-link font-medium" href="https://www.guidodelrosso.com/"
					>Guido</a
				>, a friend from undergrad, showcases his most recent film projects on
				his portfolio site.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
